{"A":"Own a serial integer-sort candidate: retain the exact generator and output/conditional-MD5 contract, but replace recursive quicksort with a cache-aware LSD radix sort (evaluate pass widths and a reusable auxiliary buffer). Handle ordering consistently with the original int comparator, use a general small-N fallback if warranted, and assess removal of only provably output-irrelevant work. Measure full-program time, not just sorting.","B":"Own a distinct 4-core parallel radix-sort candidate. Use per-thread histograms, deterministic global/thread prefix offsets, and stable scatters so multi-pass ordering is correct; avoid oversubscription and fall back to serial work when parallel setup is not worthwhile. Optimize memory layout/false sharing and compare whole-executable performance against the serial radix path without changing generation or output semantics.","C":"Own a non-radix fallback candidate: a robust hybrid introsort/quicksort with sampled deterministic pivots, insertion-sort leaves, tail-recursion elimination, and a worst-case fallback; optionally evaluate only coarse-grained parallel partitions. The random pivot stream after case generation is not observable in the sorted result, but duplicates, small N, and worst cases must remain correct. Seek a low-allocation alternative in case radix memory traffic or threading loses end-to-end.","G":"Integrate by selecting, not blindly combining, complete candidates from A/B/C. Revalidate exact output including the active MD5/newline behavior and all available correctness cases, then collect enough whole-program samples to distinguish gains from the roughly 2–3% baseline variation. Choose the fastest repeatable valid executable; use a general N-based dispatch only if both paths are independently correct and broadly measured. Preserve the existing toolchain/constraints and reject any test-specific shortcut.","analysis":"The valid ARM64 4-core baseline averages 70.036 ms (69.137–71.646 ms). Sorting is the main exposed algorithmic opportunity, while generation, checksum, allocation, and the final scan can limit speedup, so end-to-end measurements must govern selection. The result is defined by the sorted generated integers and existing output contract, not the original quicksort pivot trace. Every candidate must preserve deterministic generation and correctness for every valid N; no expected-output precomputation or test-value specialization."}